EXPERIMENT 1 (D1): GRASSMANNIAN CEILING ROBUSTNESS UNDER CONTINUOUS RELAXATION
==========================================================================================
  n=4, entries={0,1}, N= 2048 | det!=0: 0.3540 | perm!=0: 0.4814 | gap: +0.1274
  n=4, entries=F_3  , N= 2048 | det!=0: 0.5840 | perm!=0: 0.6113 | gap: +0.0273
  n=5, entries={0,1}, N= 2048 | det!=0: 0.3672 | perm!=0: 0.5190 | gap: +0.1519
  n=5, entries=F_3  , N= 2048 | det!=0: 0.5571 | perm!=0: 0.6382 | gap: +0.0811

  [ANALYSIS]: When entries expand from {0,1} to full F_3:
  - The Grassmannian ceiling BREAKS: all subspaces of Gr(2, n, F_3) become reachable!
  - Determinant density increases to match permanent density!
  - The separation is SPECIFIC to the {0,1} restriction!
  [D1 BARRIER STATUS]: The Grassmannian rank separation is an artifact of
  the Boolean input restriction and does NOT generalize to arbitrary field inputs.

