EXPERIMENT 2 (D1): KOSZUL ANNIHILATOR T^{(4)} ROBUSTNESS UNDER NILPOTENT PERTURBATION
==========================================================================================
  delta =     0 | D=6 rank of (perm_4 + delta*det_4) on L_9: 2250 / 3003 (corank = 753)
  delta =     1 | D=6 rank of (perm_4 + delta*det_4) on L_9: 2340 / 3003 (corank = 663)
  delta =   100 | D=6 rank of (perm_4 + delta*det_4) on L_9: 2414 / 3003 (corank = 589)
  delta =  1000 | D=6 rank of (perm_4 + delta*det_4) on L_9: 2414 / 3003 (corank = 589)

  [ANALYSIS]: The Koszul D=6 rank of perm_4 + delta * det_4 changes with delta.
  When delta is large enough that det_4 dominates, rank may change dramatically.
  The annihilator T^{(4)} is NOT a topological invariant: it depends on the
  specific polynomial, and mixing perm with det can degrade separation.
  [D1 BARRIER STATUS]: T^{(4)} separation is polynomial-specific, not family-generic.

